{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>Upon the altar, lambs of</b> — ס\"ת (end-letters of the phrase): לחמי (my bread)." "<b>Year, two</b> — ר\"ת (initial letters) and ס\"ת (final letters): השמש (the sun), for they would slaughter it facing the sun. Written here: שנים ליום תמיד, and in Pinchas he added to say: שנים ליום עולה תמיד — qere in it: ליום עולה, meaning: corresponding to the sun. שניים ליום תמיד — ר\"ת: עולה תש\"ל, the numerical value of תש\"ל is 365, the daily offerings were sacrificed for 365 days."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The ס\"ת abbreviation refers to the final letters of the preceding Hebrew phrase, which spell לחמי.", 1 "The text plays on reading ליום עולה as 'corresponding to the sun' (יום עולה = the day rises, i.e., the sun). The ר\"ת of שניים ליום תמיד yields של\"ת or similar; the text reads עולה תש\"ל, likely a notarikon expansion. The gematria of תש\"ל = 400+300+30+30 = 760, but the text states 365, which equals שמש (sun); the argument links the notarikon to the sun and to 365 days. Preserved exactly as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:45.405231984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}